// A type parameter of the RECEIVER must not be collected as one of the
// METHOD's own -- not when the receiver is written bare, with its type
// arguments left to inference.
//
//     type mutable Boxed[R Mark](value R);
//     given[R Mark] Boxed[R] {
//         public stat(r R) Int = { return r.mark(); };
//     };
//     Boxed.stat(Small(7));        -- R is the receiver's, not the method's
//
// For the bare spelling no receiver type arguments are written, so the lookup
// that classifies generic names found `R` unbound and filed it under the
// method. `stat` declares ZERO method type parameters, so the call then
// carried one type argument too many. mono's arity check bailed to
// `Symbol(DefId(0))`, and codegen emitted a call whose C name is the empty
// string -- the body was never monomorphized at all:
//
//     intptr_t _t68 = (__mir_tmp_0_0);
//
// The written spelling `Boxed[Small].stat(...)` was always fine: there `R` is
// bound from the written arguments and the classification is right. That is
// also why a single explicit call ANYWHERE in the program masks the defect --
// it lays down a correct entry the bare call then reuses.
//
// The constructor case is `generic_given_constructor_inference_regression`.
// This one deliberately has no construction in it: the trigger is the bare
// static-call form, not anything about building a value. It is also not about
// managed types -- the value-typed `Boxed` below fails the same way.

trait Mark {
    mark(self) Int;
};

type Small(v Int);

given Small as Mark {
    public mark(self) Int = self.v;
};

// Managed, and a method that does not construct anything.
type mutable MBoxed[R Mark](value R);

given[R Mark] MBoxed[R] {
    public stat(r R) Int = {
        return r.mark();
    };
};

// Value-typed. Same shape, different layout -- the defect does not care.
type VBoxed[R Mark](value R);

given[R Mark] VBoxed[R] {
    public new(r R) VBoxed[R] = {
        return VBoxed[R](r);
    };

    public get(self) R = self.value;
};

let main() Int = {
    println(MBoxed.stat(Small(1)).to_string());

    let v = VBoxed.new(Small(2));
    println(v.get().mark().to_string());

    return 0;
};
